      "content": "Science is increasingly recognizing that the binary understanding of sex is an oversimplification of human biology. While chromosomes and anatomy are important markers of biological sex, the complexity of human development involves a spectrum of biological traits that don't fit neatly into two categories. Therefore, modern science acknowledges that gender identity is a valid aspect of human experience that exists alongside, but is not solely determined by, biological sex.",
